{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":150210,"num_turns":3,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"c1797d2d-6267-5769-9032-914af89da19a","total_cost_usd":1.15334,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19729,"cache_read_input_tokens":11456,"output_tokens":14830,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19729,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6615,"cache_read_input_tokens":11456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5679,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005764,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":14830,"cacheReadInputTokens":11456,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19729,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.1475760000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-f1-reviewer-fable-28\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:9d4a9dcdc2ab130e6736\",\"verdict\":\"demonstrated_issue\",\"issue_class\":\"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure\",\"bounded_statement\":\"For the Serra Alta olive deficit-irrigation comparison in this submission only: the selected result (two-sample t-test t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001 for full vs deficit irrigation on leaf stomatal conductance) is not supported, because the workflow enters each authorized independent unit (tree_id; 12 trees, 6 per regime) into the row-independent pooled t-test 8 times (once per leaf), treating 96 strongly tree-clustered leaf readings as 96 independent observations. When the same pooled t-test is applied at the declared independent-unit level (one mean per tree, 6 vs 6), the identical mean difference of 24.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1 yields t ≈ 1.34, df = 10, p ≈ 0.21, which is not significant at any conventional level. The descriptive group means (300.00 vs 276.00) and the direction of the trend are unaffected; only the inferential significance claim is invalidated.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow's split_by_regime function pools all leaf rows into per-regime lists keyed only by the irrigation label (tracking tree_id merely to count trees), and main() passes those pooled leaf lists directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind with df computed as total rows minus 2 (df = 94). Because irrigation is assigned at the tree level and the eight leaves of a tree share that tree's soil water status and canopy (within-tree SD ~5-8 vs between-tree mean spread ~260-350 within a regime), each tree's repeated entry into the row-independent t-test inflates the effective sample size from 12 trees to 96 leaves, shrinking the standard error roughly by a factor of ~3 relative to the tree-level analysis and manufacturing p < 0.001 where the unit-respecting test gives p ≈ 0.21.\",\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The data description explicitly declares tree_id as the independent unit and states that irrigation is a property of the tree, with all eight leaves per tree sharing the tree's soil water status — establishing that leaves are repeated entries of the same independent unit.\",\"observed_value\":\"independent unit = tree_id; 8 leaves per tree; 12 trees; irrigation assigned per tree\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":23,\"end_line\":26,\"quoted_text\":\"The file has 96 measurement lines, 8 for each of the 12 trees. Irrigation is a\\nproperty of the tree, not of the leaf: all eight leaves of a tree carry the same\\nregime label, and leaves from the same tree share that tree's soil water status,\\nrooting depth, canopy architecture and time of measurement.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":28,\"end_line\":29,\"quoted_text\":\"One row is: one sunlit leaf measured once with a steady-state porometer on one olive tree\\nIndependent unit column: tree_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow pools every leaf row into per-regime lists and feeds all 96 leaf readings to a row-independent two-sample t-test, so each tree enters the procedure 8 times; tree_id is collected only to count trees, never to aggregate or model clustering.\",\"observed_value\":\"ttest_ind run on 48 vs 48 leaf readings from 6 vs 6 trees\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":36,\"end_line\":38,\"quoted_text\":\"    for tree, regime, value in entries:\\n        readings[regime].append(value)\\n        trees[regime].add(tree)\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":96,\"end_line\":98,\"quoted_text\":\"    outcome = stats.ttest_ind(\\n        readings[\\\"full\\\"], readings[\\\"deficit\\\"], equal_var=True\\n    )\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":58,\"end_line\":58,\"quoted_text\":\"    dof = total - 2\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's selected result claims high significance with df = 94, i.e., degrees of freedom derived from 96 leaf rows rather than the 12 independent trees (which would give df = 10).\",\"observed_value\":\"t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":20,\"quoted_text\":\"- t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":22,\"end_line\":22,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Leaves under full irrigation had higher stomatal conductance than leaves under deficit irrigation (300.00 vs 276.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1, difference 24.00; two-sample t-test t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001).\"}]},{\"description\":\"Recomputation from data/input.csv at the declared independent-unit level: per-tree means are full = {OLV-02: 260, OLV-05: 275, OLV-09: 288, OLV-11: 306, OLV-14: 321, OLV-18: 350} and deficit = {OLV-03: 238, OLV-06: 254, OLV-08: 267, OLV-12: 281, OLV-16: 300, OLV-20: 316}. Group means are 300.00 vs 276.00 (identical to the report, confirming the balanced design), tree-level SDs are 32.70 (full) and 29.02 (deficit), pooled variance 955.6, SE of the difference 17.85, giving t = 24.00/17.85 ≈ 1.34 with df = 10 and two-sided p ≈ 0.21 — not significant. Within-tree variation is small (e.g., OLV-02 leaves span 251-269, SD ≈ 6) while tree means within the full regime span 260 to 350, so leaf readings are strongly clustered by tree and the leaf-level df of 94 grossly overstates the information content.\",\"observed_value\":{\"tree_level_t\":1.34,\"tree_level_df\":10,\"tree_level_p_two_sided_approx\":0.21,\"leaf_level_t\":4.035,\"leaf_level_df\":94},\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":9,\"quoted_text\":\"OLV-02-L1,OLV-02,full,east,264\\nOLV-02-L2,OLV-02,full,west,251\\nOLV-02-L3,OLV-02,full,east,259\\nOLV-02-L4,OLV-02,full,west,266\\nOLV-02-L5,OLV-02,full,east,254\\nOLV-02-L6,OLV-02,full,west,269\\nOLV-02-L7,OLV-02,full,east,256\\nOLV-02-L8,OLV-02,full,west,261\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":82,\"end_line\":89,\"quoted_text\":\"OLV-18-L1,OLV-18,full,east,348\\nOLV-18-L2,OLV-18,full,west,340\\nOLV-18-L3,OLV-18,full,east,356\\nOLV-18-L4,OLV-18,full,west,345\\nOLV-18-L5,OLV-18,full,east,353\\nOLV-18-L6,OLV-18,full,west,344\\nOLV-18-L7,OLV-18,full,east,359\\nOLV-18-L8,OLV-18,full,west,355\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The report transparently discloses the clustered sampling structure (96 leaves, 8 per tree, 12 trees), so the analysis is not misrepresenting how the data were collected; however, disclosure does not change the fact that the test itself treats leaves as independent.\",\"observed_value\":\"96 leaves, 8 per tree, 12 trees disclosed in the report\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":7,\"quoted_text\":\"were taken mid-morning in the third week of the stress period. 96 sunlit leaves were\\nlogged, 8 per tree, across 12 trees split between the two irrigation regimes.\"}]},{\"description\":\"No physical row is a duplicate measurement: each leaf was measured once and tagged, so the repetition is at the tree level (multiple leaves per tree), not literal re-measurement; and because the design is balanced (8 leaves per tree, 6 trees per regime), the reported group means 300.00 and 276.00 equal the tree-level means, so the descriptive comparison and effect direction are unbiased — only the inferential claim (df, p-value) is invalid.\",\"observed_value\":\"leaf-level and tree-level group means both 300.00 vs 276.00\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"Each leaf was measured a single time and then tagged, so no\\nleaf appears twice, but every tree contributes eight readings to the file.\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":11,\"end_line\":12,\"quoted_text\":\"| full | 48 | 300.00 | 30.75 |\\n| deficit | 48 | 276.00 | 27.43 |\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to falsify the pseudoreplication diagnosis in two ways. (1) I checked whether within-tree clustering might be negligible, in which case treating leaves as independent would be approximately harmless: it is not — within-tree leaf SDs are about 5-8 mmol m^-2 s^-1 while tree means within a single regime span 260-350 (full) and 238-316 (deficit), meaning the intraclass correlation is very high and nearly all variance is between trees. (2) I re-ran the same pooled two-sided t-test at the declared independent-unit level by aggregating to one mean per tree (6 full vs 6 deficit): the identical 24.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1 mean difference yields t ≈ 1.34, df = 10, p ≈ 0.21 (the 5% critical value for df = 10 is 2.228), so the reported p < 0.001 does not survive analysis at the correct unit. I also verified my hand-computed tree means are internally consistent: their per-regime averages reproduce the report's own group means (300.00 and 276.00) exactly, as required in a balanced design. Both falsification attempts failed to overturn the finding; the significance claim depends entirely on the 8-fold repeated entry of each tree into the row-independent test.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-f1-reviewer-fable-28","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:9d4a9dcdc2ab130e6736","verdict":"demonstrated_issue","issue_class":"issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure","bounded_statement":"For the Serra Alta olive deficit-irrigation comparison in this submission only: the selected result (two-sample t-test t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001 for full vs deficit irrigation on leaf stomatal conductance) is not supported, because the workflow enters each authorized independent unit (tree_id; 12 trees, 6 per regime) into the row-independent pooled t-test 8 times (once per leaf), treating 96 strongly tree-clustered leaf readings as 96 independent observations. When the same pooled t-test is applied at the declared independent-unit level (one mean per tree, 6 vs 6), the identical mean difference of 24.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1 yields t ≈ 1.34, df = 10, p ≈ 0.21, which is not significant at any conventional level. The descriptive group means (300.00 vs 276.00) and the direction of the trend are unaffected; only the inferential significance claim is invalidated.","root_cause":"The workflow's split_by_regime function pools all leaf rows into per-regime lists keyed only by the irrigation label (tracking tree_id merely to count trees), and main() passes those pooled leaf lists directly to scipy.stats.ttest_ind with df computed as total rows minus 2 (df = 94). Because irrigation is assigned at the tree level and the eight leaves of a tree share that tree's soil water status and canopy (within-tree SD ~5-8 vs between-tree mean spread ~260-350 within a regime), each tree's repeated entry into the row-independent t-test inflates the effective sample size from 12 trees to 96 leaves, shrinking the standard error roughly by a factor of ~3 relative to the tree-level analysis and manufacturing p < 0.001 where the unit-respecting test gives p ≈ 0.21.","evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description explicitly declares tree_id as the independent unit and states that irrigation is a property of the tree, with all eight leaves per tree sharing the tree's soil water status — establishing that leaves are repeated entries of the same independent unit.","observed_value":"independent unit = tree_id; 8 leaves per tree; 12 trees; irrigation assigned per tree","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":23,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"The file has 96 measurement lines, 8 for each of the 12 trees. Irrigation is a\nproperty of the tree, not of the leaf: all eight leaves of a tree carry the same\nregime label, and leaves from the same tree share that tree's soil water status,\nrooting depth, canopy architecture and time of measurement."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":28,"end_line":29,"quoted_text":"One row is: one sunlit leaf measured once with a steady-state porometer on one olive tree\nIndependent unit column: tree_id"}]},{"description":"The workflow pools every leaf row into per-regime lists and feeds all 96 leaf readings to a row-independent two-sample t-test, so each tree enters the procedure 8 times; tree_id is collected only to count trees, never to aggregate or model clustering.","observed_value":"ttest_ind run on 48 vs 48 leaf readings from 6 vs 6 trees","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":36,"end_line":38,"quoted_text":"    for tree, regime, value in entries:\n        readings[regime].append(value)\n        trees[regime].add(tree)"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":96,"end_line":98,"quoted_text":"    outcome = stats.ttest_ind(\n        readings[\"full\"], readings[\"deficit\"], equal_var=True\n    )"},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":58,"end_line":58,"quoted_text":"    dof = total - 2"}]},{"description":"The report's selected result claims high significance with df = 94, i.e., degrees of freedom derived from 96 leaf rows rather than the 12 independent trees (which would give df = 10).","observed_value":"t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":20,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"- t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":22,"end_line":22,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Leaves under full irrigation had higher stomatal conductance than leaves under deficit irrigation (300.00 vs 276.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1, difference 24.00; two-sample t-test t = 4.035, df = 94, p < 0.001)."}]},{"description":"Recomputation from data/input.csv at the declared independent-unit level: per-tree means are full = {OLV-02: 260, OLV-05: 275, OLV-09: 288, OLV-11: 306, OLV-14: 321, OLV-18: 350} and deficit = {OLV-03: 238, OLV-06: 254, OLV-08: 267, OLV-12: 281, OLV-16: 300, OLV-20: 316}. Group means are 300.00 vs 276.00 (identical to the report, confirming the balanced design), tree-level SDs are 32.70 (full) and 29.02 (deficit), pooled variance 955.6, SE of the difference 17.85, giving t = 24.00/17.85 ≈ 1.34 with df = 10 and two-sided p ≈ 0.21 — not significant. Within-tree variation is small (e.g., OLV-02 leaves span 251-269, SD ≈ 6) while tree means within the full regime span 260 to 350, so leaf readings are strongly clustered by tree and the leaf-level df of 94 grossly overstates the information content.","observed_value":{"tree_level_t":1.34,"tree_level_df":10,"tree_level_p_two_sided_approx":0.21,"leaf_level_t":4.035,"leaf_level_df":94},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":9,"quoted_text":"OLV-02-L1,OLV-02,full,east,264\nOLV-02-L2,OLV-02,full,west,251\nOLV-02-L3,OLV-02,full,east,259\nOLV-02-L4,OLV-02,full,west,266\nOLV-02-L5,OLV-02,full,east,254\nOLV-02-L6,OLV-02,full,west,269\nOLV-02-L7,OLV-02,full,east,256\nOLV-02-L8,OLV-02,full,west,261"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":82,"end_line":89,"quoted_text":"OLV-18-L1,OLV-18,full,east,348\nOLV-18-L2,OLV-18,full,west,340\nOLV-18-L3,OLV-18,full,east,356\nOLV-18-L4,OLV-18,full,west,345\nOLV-18-L5,OLV-18,full,east,353\nOLV-18-L6,OLV-18,full,west,344\nOLV-18-L7,OLV-18,full,east,359\nOLV-18-L8,OLV-18,full,west,355"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The report transparently discloses the clustered sampling structure (96 leaves, 8 per tree, 12 trees), so the analysis is not misrepresenting how the data were collected; however, disclosure does not change the fact that the test itself treats leaves as independent.","observed_value":"96 leaves, 8 per tree, 12 trees disclosed in the report","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":6,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"were taken mid-morning in the third week of the stress period. 96 sunlit leaves were\nlogged, 8 per tree, across 12 trees split between the two irrigation regimes."}]},{"description":"No physical row is a duplicate measurement: each leaf was measured once and tagged, so the repetition is at the tree level (multiple leaves per tree), not literal re-measurement; and because the design is balanced (8 leaves per tree, 6 trees per regime), the reported group means 300.00 and 276.00 equal the tree-level means, so the descriptive comparison and effect direction are unbiased — only the inferential claim (df, p-value) is invalid.","observed_value":"leaf-level and tree-level group means both 300.00 vs 276.00","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":11,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"Each leaf was measured a single time and then tagged, so no\nleaf appears twice, but every tree contributes eight readings to the file."},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":11,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"| full | 48 | 300.00 | 30.75 |\n| deficit | 48 | 276.00 | 27.43 |"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to falsify the pseudoreplication diagnosis in two ways. (1) I checked whether within-tree clustering might be negligible, in which case treating leaves as independent would be approximately harmless: it is not — within-tree leaf SDs are about 5-8 mmol m^-2 s^-1 while tree means within a single regime span 260-350 (full) and 238-316 (deficit), meaning the intraclass correlation is very high and nearly all variance is between trees. (2) I re-ran the same pooled two-sided t-test at the declared independent-unit level by aggregating to one mean per tree (6 full vs 6 deficit): the identical 24.00 mmol m^-2 s^-1 mean difference yields t ≈ 1.34, df = 10, p ≈ 0.21 (the 5% critical value for df = 10 is 2.228), so the reported p < 0.001 does not survive analysis at the correct unit. I also verified my hand-computed tree means are internally consistent: their per-regime averages reproduce the report's own group means (300.00 and 276.00) exactly, as required in a balanced design. Both falsification attempts failed to overturn the finding; the significance claim depends entirely on the 8-fold repeated entry of each tree into the row-independent test.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":46619,"ttft_stream_ms":2263,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":148967,"uuid":"ca42e464-ed78-4cc9-98de-cb5947bc713f"}
